~ introCutscene
set Player.canMove = false
Mort: "..."
Mort: "The bed feels less empty than it did yesterday."
Mort: "Since when did I get so used to Harry not being here?"
Mort: "..."
Mort: "I need to get out of bed."
Mort: "But I can't stop thinking about that book Harry left behind."
Mort: "Can it really..?"
Mort: "Ugh, I swear I'm going insane. I need to get out of the house..."
Mort: "Even if I have to talk to those #######s."

Press 'E' to interact. An item is interactable when an exclamation mark appears over your head.
set Player.canMove = true
=> END

~ RyanDayZero
set Player.canMove = false
set NPC.tempElapTime = NPC.elapsedTime
set NPC.tempCycProg = NPC.cycleProgress

Ryan: "Well Howdy there, neighbor! How's your morning been?"
Hostility, immediately.
Mort: "Just dandy, Ryan. Just dandy."
Mort: "Say, I know this is a longshot, but do you recognize this book?"
I showed Ryan the book.
Ryan: "Well, I don't particularly say I do, now. What's it about? Maybe I've heard from a friend about it."
I can feel the malice dripping from his every word.
Mort: "It seems like some recipe book, I was wondering if Harry had ever talked to you about it."
Ryan: "Nosiree, not me. That Harry sure was a gem, though."
A look of false pity falls over his expression.
Ryan: "You know, Mort, if you ever need something, just let me know, okay?"
Ryan: "Don't be a stranger, now."
As if I would believe that.
Mort: "Sure thing, Ryan. I'll see you around."
set Player.dayZeroMarker += 1

set NPC.elapsedTime = NPC.tempElapTime
set NPC.cycleProgress = NPC.tempCycProg
set NPC.isIdle = false
set NPC.canMove = true
set Player.canMove = true
=> END

~ JudithDayZero
set Player.canMove = false
set NPC.tempElapTime = NPC.elapsedTime
set NPC.tempCycProg = NPC.cycleProgress

Mort: "Good morning, Judith. You didn't have any trouble getting out of bed this morning, did you?"
Though it would have been nice to know she had a bad morning, it's good she didnt.
I needed to talk to her, and I sure as hell wasn't going inside her house.
Judith: "Oh good morning to you too, Mort. I know I don't look it, but I'm still young and spry!"
Judith: "Oh that reminds me!"
Judith handed me a muffin.
Judith: "I had extra this morning and you know how poorly muffins last."
Judith: "I'd much rather have a young man like you eat his fill than have it go to waste."
With a tight smile, I took the muffin and shoved it in my pocket.
Mort: "Oh thanks Judith, this'll make me feel right as rain!"
Mort: "By the way, speaking of young and old, you've seen a couple more years than me, do you recognize this book?"
I showed Judith the book.
Judith: "Let me put on my spectacles and take a look..."
After a quick once-over...
Judith: "Oh, I'm sorry Mort, I don't think I have. Then again, my memory isn't the best these days."
Judith: "You and Harry take care now, won't you?"
That horrid old woman.
Mort: "Haha sure can do, Judith. See you around!"
set Player.dayZeroMarker += 1

set NPC.elapsedTime = NPC.tempElapTime
set NPC.cycleProgress = NPC.tempCycProg
set NPC.isIdle = false
set NPC.canMove = true
set Player.canMove = true
=> END

~ ChrisDayZero
set Player.canMove = false
set NPC.tempElapTime = NPC.elapsedTime
set NPC.tempCycProg = NPC.cycleProgress

Before I can even get a word out, Chris's boisterous voice hits me full force.
Chris: "Hey Mr. Mort! I haven't seen you in a while!"
Having jogged towards me at a fast pace, Chris seems to barely be breaking a sweat, like it was nothing to him.
Mort: "Spry as ever, are we Chris? It's so early and you're already running all over the place."
If he smiled any wider it'd look uncanny.
Chris: "Of course I am! Gotta stay as healthy as I can so I can live as long as possible!"
It wasn't long before Chris realized what he said.
Chris: "Ah- sorry Mr. Mort, I didn't mean to-"
Mort: "None taken. Anyways, you ever see this book on the web?"
I showed Chris the book, which he seemed to take all too eagerly as a way out of the hole he dug himself.
However, he appeared crestfallen soonafter.
Chris: "Sorry, Mr. Mort. I've never been much of a reader, so I doubt I'd know about it."
Chris: "Say, isn't necromancy that-"
I yanked the book back away from him.
Mort: "Thank you for your time, Chris. You can get back to... whatever you were doing before."
Before he could even respond, I quickly took off.
set Player.dayZeroMarker += 1

set NPC.elapsedTime = NPC.tempElapTime
set NPC.cycleProgress = NPC.tempCycProg
set NPC.isIdle = false
set NPC.canMove = true
set Player.canMove = true
=> END

~ AgathaDayZero
set Player.canMove = false
set NPC.tempElapTime = NPC.elapsedTime
set NPC.tempCycProg = NPC.cycleProgress

Agatha: "Mortimer."
Agatha nodded towards me curtly. She was always here, in front of her house, making sure the town was safe.
She was always here.
Mort: "Agatha."
I nodded back. If you didn't deal with Agatha with caution, you wouldn't get much out of her.
Mort: "I'll get straight to the point. Do you recognize this book at all?"
I don't even need to offer it to her. She takes the book from me in one swift motion.
Agatha: "Never seen this in my life, Mortimer. You're not getting into all that supernatural nonsense, now are you? I thought more of you."
Her hardened expression melted into one of sympathy. It didn't fit her.
Agatha: "You know all of us in the village are here for you, right? We're still a family."
As Agatha spoke, she handed the book back to me.
Mort: "Thank you Agatha, I'll try to keep that in mind."
I turn and leave curtly, not seeing if she had any sort of reaction.
set Player.dayZeroMarker += 1

set NPC.elapsedTime = NPC.tempElapTime
set NPC.cycleProgress = NPC.tempCycProg
set NPC.isIdle = false
set NPC.canMove = true
set Player.canMove = true
=> END

~ AlreadyTalked
set Player.canMove = false

if !NPC.deathFlag 
	I've already talked to them today, and once was more than I could bear.
else
	Please just go down quietly...

set Player.canMove = true
=> END

~ EndOfDayZeroCutscene
set Player.canMove = false

if (Player.dayZeroMarker >= 4):
	I've talked to everyone today, and none of them recognized the book. If Harry hasn't showed it to any of them, maybe he meant to leave it for me...
	Those #######s let him die, whether they'll admit it or not. If the recipes in this book are what it takes to bring him back, they can all rot.
	Anything to bring Harry back...
	From the Dead...
	
	set IM.dayCounter = 1
	do IM.emit_signal("changeItems")
	set Player.canMove = true
else:
	I haven't talked to everyone just yet, I still need to see if any of them recognize Harry's book.
	set Player.canMove = true

=> END
